# GitHub Personal Access Token(s) used to query the GitHub API.
# Add as many as you like (PAT_1, PAT_2, ...) — the app rotates through
# them when one is rate-limited. A classic token with no scopes is enough
# for public data; add "repo" + "read:user" scopes to show private stats.
PAT_1=

# Optional: comma-separated list of GitHub usernames allowed to use this
# instance. Leave unset to allow anyone.
# WHITELIST=

# Optional: comma-separated list of gist owners allowed to use /api/gist.
# GIST_WHITELIST=

# Optional: comma-separated list of repos to always exclude from stats.
# EXCLUDE_REPO=
